+/* Memory-read reply layouts, as measured on the two firmware generations.
+ *
+ * Older firmware (11033/14003) answers with the data straight after the
+ * command byte:  cmd(1) + len16(2) + data + cksum(1).
+ *
+ * Firmware 14115 (MateBook 13 WRT-WX9, this unit) prepends an echo of the
+ * request — the 4-byte address, the 4-byte length and the request checksum —
+ * and counts that overhead inside the requested length:
+ *
+ *   cmd(1) + len16(2) + addr_echo(4) + len_echo(4) + req_cksum(1)
+ *   + data(N-9) + reply_cksum(1)
